1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,075
NGOs have thousands of scattered field photos.

2
00:00:03,075 --> 00:00:07,821
When a funder asks, what changed?, someone digs through phones by hand.

3
00:00:07,821 --> 00:00:13,704
Ground Truth turns those photos into organized, traceable evidence, built on Cloudinary.

4
00:00:14,105 --> 00:00:18,439
The app follows four steps: collect, explore, review, and share.

5
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:24,197
This demo has four projects, eight images, and four confirmed before-and-after pairs.

6
00:00:24,197 --> 00:00:28,464
And the banner says it upfront: the after images are AI-edited,

7
00:00:28,464 --> 00:00:31,241
and the sites and dates are illustrative.

8
00:00:31,842 --> 00:00:37,665
In the Evidence library, every photo is stored on Cloudinary and grouped by project.

9
00:00:37,665 --> 00:00:43,142
The AI wrote each caption and activity type, and they're labelled AI-suggested.

10
00:00:43,142 --> 00:00:49,381
These thumbnails are Cloudinary transformations: auto-crop, auto-quality, and auto-format.

11
00:00:49,381 --> 00:00:52,986
Filters narrow things down by project or photo type.

12
00:00:54,511 --> 00:00:56,153
Search lives right here.

13
00:00:56,153 --> 00:00:58,616
Let's type: tangled wires on a wall.

14
00:00:58,616 --> 00:01:02,380
With an AI key, this searches by meaning, not keywords.

15
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:08,128
This recording runs the key-free demo, so it falls back to keyword and tag matching,

16
00:01:08,128 --> 00:01:09,497
and it tells you so.

17
00:01:09,497 --> 00:01:12,576
Either way, every result says why it matched.

18
00:01:12,576 --> 00:01:14,287
Now: damaged drain cover.

19
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:21,947
On Review pairs, the system suggests before-and-after pairs from location, visual similarity,

20
00:01:21,947 --> 00:01:22,989
and time order.

21
00:01:22,989 --> 00:01:24,586
It never auto-confirms.

22
00:01:24,586 --> 00:01:25,767
A person decides.

23
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:27,919
Here's the Vyttila wiring pair.

24
00:01:27,919 --> 00:01:31,114
Drag the slider to see the visible difference.

25
00:01:31,714 --> 00:01:36,468
Here's the score breakdown, and the exact Cloudinary URLs behind the slider.

26
00:01:36,468 --> 00:01:41,410
The campaign card is a shareable image built entirely from Cloudinary overlays.

27
00:01:43,013 --> 00:01:44,206
The Impact report.

28
00:01:44,206 --> 00:01:46,990
The counts come from the data, not the AI.

29
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:53,087
The summary is written only from stored facts, and every image it cites is checked to exist.

30
00:01:53,087 --> 00:01:54,943
This green check shows that.

31
00:01:54,943 --> 00:01:59,981
Here's the timeline, the evidence table, and one click downloads the report.

32
00:02:03,346 --> 00:02:05,615
Finally, Trace, on a gutter image.

33
00:02:05,615 --> 00:02:07,216
The Cloudinary original.

34
00:02:07,216 --> 00:02:11,354
The capture date, location, and where that metadata came from.

35
00:02:11,354 --> 00:02:13,890
The full AI output and the model used.

36
00:02:13,890 --> 00:02:19,162
And the transformation chain: every Cloudinary URL the app delivered is logged.

37
00:02:20,364 --> 00:02:26,259
Ground Truth flags near-duplicates and missing location or date, blurs faces on delivery,

38
00:02:26,259 --> 00:02:28,445
and never claims verified impact.

39
00:02:28,445 --> 00:02:32,485
It only shows the visible difference between confirmed pairs.

40
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:37,519
In this demo, the after images are AI-edited and the sites are illustrative,

41
00:02:37,519 --> 00:02:38,844
and the app says so.
